{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgt2m5eg3DEr7VJaK7nAt","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Two problems with this attempt. First, `tok.decode` silently dropped the special tokens (`<|im_start|>`, `<think>`, …), so these texts don't match the eval format. Second, and more important, the window for geometry_151 contains no verbatim loop, even though my detector placed the onset at token 615. The cause is a flaw in the detector: requiring ≥95% repeats from the onset to the end lets a ~30k-token loop tail absorb up to ~1,500 earlier non-repeated tokens, so onsets were biased early. I'll redefine the onset as the start of the final contiguous run of repeated 32-grams (merging gaps under 32 tokens) and redo the onset/hazard numbers. Then I'll rebuild texts from the raw strings rather than decoded tokens. If the corrected onsets shift later, the per-1k-token hazard estimates will change, but the conclusion that ~90% of samples end in absorbing loops will not.\n\n```python\n# Hypothesis: onset estimator was biased early; recompute onset as start of final contiguous repeat run.\ndef loop_stats2(ids, n=32, gap=32):\n    L = len(ids); M = L - n + 1\n    if M < 2: return None, None, 0.0\n    seen = {}; rep = np.zeros(M, dtype=bool); last = np.full(M, -1)\n    for i in range(M):\n        key = tuple(ids[i:i+n])\n        if key in seen: rep[i] = True; last[i] = seen[key]\n        seen[key] = i\n    if not rep[-1]: return None, None, rep.mean()\n    # walk back from end while gaps of non-repeats are < gap\n    i = M - 1; nonrep = 0\n    while i > 0:\n        if rep[i-1]: nonrep = 0\n        else:\n            nonrep += 1\n            if nonrep >= gap: break\n        i -= 1\n    onset = i + nonrep if nonrep >= gap else i\n    while onset < M and not rep[onset]: onset += 1\n    if M - onset < 4*n: return None, None, rep.mean()   # require a substantial tail\n    d = (np.arange(onset, M) - last[onset:]); d = d[last[onset:] >= 0]\n    per = int(np.bincount(d).argmax()) if len(d) else None\n    return onset, per, rep.mean()\nrows2 = []\nfor (pid, si), ids in IDS.items():\n    on, per, frac = loop_stats2(ids)\n    r = df[(df.id==pid)&(df.si==si)].iloc[0]\n    rows2.append(dict(id=pid, si=si, src=r.src, cut=r.cut, correct=r.correct, ntok=len(ids), onset=on, period=per))\ndf2 = pd.DataFrame(rows2)\nc2 = df2[df2.cut]\nprint('cut with loop tail:', c2.onset.notna().mean(), ' onset q:', c2.onset.quantile([.1,.25,.5,.75,.9]).round().tolist())\nprint('period q:', c2.period.quantile([.1,.25,.5,.75,.9]).tolist())\nprint('loop tail tokens median:', (c2.ntok - c2.onset).median())\n```"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3816,"cache_read_input_tokens":50214,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3816},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"37ae3ac5-393a-4da3-8caf-f8ba0ea8f929","uuid":"7687df27-7fdc-4884-b9cd-2499f6f3bb78","timestamp":"2026-11-09T21:03:39.622Z","request_id":"req_011Cgt2m54wrZMoeV4tA2qRB"}
